  +   chars (bash drops NUL, tree-sitter keeps it); backslash-space (`echo\ test`, tree-sitter's text keeps the
  +   backslash so argv[0] mismatches). Parse budget (50 ms / 50,000 nodes) — a timeout is attacker-triggerable via
  +   nested array subscripts, so it returns "too complex → ask", **never falls back to the old engine**. ~20 eval-like
  +   builtins as argv[0] (`eval`, `trap`, `coproc`, …) → ask. Array subscripts are arithmetic and expand `$(…)` even
  +   inside what looks like an opaque quoted leaf.
  + - adversa.ai: Claude Code deny rules were bypassed by padding a command past 50 subcommands (a per-subcommand
  +   checking cap) — a caution against any "check only the first N extracted commands" shortcut.
